From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:25:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: record canvas transforms and paths lazily

Extend the bounded display-list model from0030, not the browser into a
rendering engine. Both regular and offscreen2D contexts now share affine
transform composition, reset/get/setTransform, dictionary alias validation,
state save/restore, transformed rectangles/clears and synthetic glyph output.
Numeric dictionary members preserve null-to-zero coercion. putImageData and
getImageData remain independent of the current transform as required.

Record the current path in device coordinates at construction time. Reuse
SVG's existing bounded curve flattener for quadratic/cubic segments; record
moves, lines, closures, rectangles and circular arcs. Snapshot path geometry
when fill/stroke is called so subsequent path edits cannot change history.
Support nonzero/evenodd fill rules, geometric hit tests, lineWidth/lineCap
validation and saved state, plus non-mutating strokeRect. Stroke width uses
the paint-time transform; synthetic path coverage is evaluated only during
readback/serialization, through the same replay path as PNG output.

Retain axis-aligned transformed replacement pruning so animation clears
recycle prior commands and owned path snapshots. Reject non-finite inverse
samples, normalize arc sweeps without overflowing finite angle differences,
include square caps in conservative bounds, distinguish fill coverage from
boundary-inclusive hit tests, and handle zero-length round-capped segments.

This is deliberately synthetic pixel output: no GPU, Skia, external rendering
library, eager framebuffer, real font rasterization, exact antialiasing or
Chrome/Mac fingerprint hash is introduced. Path2D, clip, full stroke joins,
dash coverage, gradients/pattern painting and unrelated existing no-op APIs
remain outside this change. This does not claim complete Canvas2D rendering
conformance or a remedy for the separate Sephora catalog denial.

A temporary owned main-world fixture covers54 cases for each context type:
108/108 checks pass in the patched Debug build, Camoufox158 and Chrome154;
the saved normal0096 binary passes22/108. Checks cover matrix overloads,
coercion, save/reset, simple transformed pixels, path snapshot/fill/hit-test
semantics and review-derived numerical/coverage regressions. Matrix checks
allow1e-6 reference rounding. Stroke checks test semantic coverage rather
than antialiasing; reference engines differ on zero-length stroke pixels.
All1658 existing upstream tests pass; none were added or modified.

Reference: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#2dcontext
